  "description": "The laboratory is using the P10\u202fsingle\u2011channel pipette, version\u202f1.3 (identified as \u201cp10_single_v1.3\u201d). All motion limits are calibrated in millimetres: the plunger\u2019s top stop is set at 10\u202fmm (allowable range 0\u201312\u202fmm), the bottom stop at 0\u202fmm (0\u201312\u202fmm), and the blow\u2011out position at 11\u202fmm (0\u201312\u202fmm). The tip\u2011drop travel distance is 0.5\u202fmm (0\u20131\u202fmm). Pickup is performed with a current of 0.8\u202fA (0\u20131\u202fA) over a 0.3\u202fmm distance (0\u20135\u202fmm), using a single press, an incremental step of 0.05\u202fmm (0\u20130.5\u202fmm) and a speed of 20\u202fmm\u202fs\u207b\u00b9 (1\u2013100\u202fmm\u202fs\u207b\u00b9). Plunger actuation current is 0.6\u202fA (0\u20131\u202fA) and tip\u2011drop current is 0.5\u202fA (0\u20131\u202fA) with a drop\u2011tip speed of 30\u202fmm\u202fs\u207b\u00b9 (1\u2013150\u202fmm\u202fs\u207b\u00b9). The model offset is neutral at [0,\u202f0,\u202f0]\u202fmm, the tip length is 51.5\u202fmm, the idle current is set to 0.15\u202fA, and the tip\u2011return height after a drop is 0.5\u202fmm. Tip\u2011overlap defaults to 0.2\u202fmm, but for the Opentrons\u202f96\u2011tip\u2011rack\u202f300\u202f\u00b5L it is reduced to 0.15\u202fmm. The only registered quirk for this pipette is \u201cnozzle_check\u201d.\n\nThe liquid\u2011handling conversion tables are linear. For aspiration, the relationship is 0.1\u202f\u00b5L per mm of plunger travel with zero intercept; for dispensing, it is 0.12\u202f\u00b5L per mm with zero intercept. The configuration parameters that can be adjusted by the user are the top position, bottom position, blow\u2011out position, and pickup speed. Finally, the system recognises two valid quirks for this hardware: \u201cnozzle_check\u201d and \u201cfast_tip_pickup\u201d."
}